  "verbalization": "Tiapride is shown to have a direct target relationship with Granzyme B through two distinct pathways. In Path 1, Tiapride targets a peroxisomal bifunctional enzyme, which is subsequently targeted by Oxamic Acid, and Oxamic Acid in turn targets Granzyme B. In Path 2, Tiapride targets Inosine-5'-monophosphate dehydrogenase 2, which is targeted by a complex compound, and this complex also targets Granzyme B. Both pathways demonstrate a clear, albeit indirect, link between Tiapride and Granzyme B, suggesting that the drug may modulate Granzyme B through different molecular mechanisms. The evidence supports a potential role for Tiapride in influencing Granzyme B activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the drug-target relationship, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the specific molecular interactions involved.",
